itter":{"date":"2026-01-12T12:05:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/add chatbot 1 (#4)\n\n* feat: Add Greeter and PatientGetter components with configuration and data fetching capabilities\n\n- Implemented Greeter component to demonstrate configuration system usage.\n- Created PatientGetter component to fetch patient data from OpenMRS FHIR API.\n- Added corresponding SCSS styles for both components.\n- Developed unit tests for Greeter and PatientGetter components.\n- Established root component to integrate all features and display them.\n- Defined routes for the application and added translations for multiple languages.\n- Configured TypeScript and Webpack for the project.\n\n* feat: Add chatbot agent module with conversation UI and DHTI integration\n\n- Implemented configuration schema for the chatbot agent.\n- Created conversation display and message input components for user interaction.\n- Developed conversation component to manage message flow and DHTI service communication.\n- Added custom hook for handling DHTI service submissions.\n- Introduced patient fetching hook using SWR for efficient data retrieval.\n- Defined TypeScript models for CDS Hook requests and cards.\n- Configured routes and translations for multiple languages.\n- Set up TypeScript and Webpack configurations for the module.\n\n* feat: Update README and configuration for chatbot integration and testing setup\n\n* feat: Add DHTI display microfrontend with configuration schema and components\n\n- Created a new microfrontend package `@openmrs/esm-dhti-display` for DHTI display.\n- Added configuration schema to support `dhtiTitle` and `dhtiRoute`.\n- Implemented display component to show AI insights based on patient data.\n- Developed custom hooks for DHTI service interactions and patient fetching.\n- Included styles and translations for multiple languages.\n- Configured webpack and TypeScript for the new package.\n- Added routes configuration for integration with OpenMRS.\n\n* feat: Update yarn.lock to include chatbot agent and display packages with dependencies\n\n* feat: Update CI workflows to include develop branch and remove hourly schedule for dependency updates\n\n* feat: Update README to include DHTI project details, setup instructions, and contributing guidelines\n\n* feat: Update CI workflows to use workflow_dispatch and add main.yml for build process\n\n* feat: Add axios as a dependency in package.json\n\n* Implement feature X to enhance user experience and fix bug Y in module Z\n\n* Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability","tree":{"sha":"bb25ed0666daf27780bccfeb0789454097289972","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dermatologist/openmrs-esm-dhti/git/trees/bb25ed0666daf27780bccfeb0789454097289972"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dermatologist/openmrs-esm-dhti/git/commits/19992a34479a7d442794b54fbbc0861dadb45ada","verification":{"payload":"tree bb25ed0666daf27780bccfeb0789454097289972\nparent 727a7d835edad6145cfd794365289f612c4216b9\nauthor Bell Eapen <github_public@gulfdoctor.net> 1768219515 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1768219515 -0600\n\nFeature/add chatbot 1 (#4)\n\n* feat: Add Greeter and PatientGetter components with configuration and data fetching capabilities\n\n- Implemented Greeter component to demonstrate configuration system usage.\n- Created PatientGetter component to fetch patient data from OpenMRS FHIR API.\n- Added corresponding SCSS styles for both components.\n- Developed unit tests for Greeter and PatientGetter components.\n- Established root component to integrate all features and display them.\n- Defined routes for the application and added translations for multiple languages.\n- Configured TypeScript and Webpack for the project.\n\n* feat: Add chatbot agent module with conversation UI and DHTI integration\n\n- Implemented configuration schema for the chatbot agent.\n- Created conversation display and message input components for user interaction.\n- Developed conversation component to manage message flow and DHTI service communication.\n- Added custom hook for handling DHTI service submissions.\n- Introduced patient fetching hook using SWR for efficient data retrieval.\n- Defined TypeScript models for CDS Hook requests and cards.\n- Configured routes and translations for multiple languages.\n- Set up TypeScript and Webpack configurations for the module.\n\n* feat: Update README and configuration for chatbot integration and testing setup\n\n* feat: Add DHTI display microfrontend with configuration schema and components\n\n- Created a new microfrontend package `@openmrs/esm-dhti-display` for DHTI display.\n- Added configuration schema to support `dhtiTitle` and `dhtiRoute`.\n- Implemented display component to show AI insights based on patient data.\n- Developed custom hooks for DHTI service interactions and patient fetching.\n- Included styles and translations for multiple languages.\n- Configured webpack and TypeScript for the new package.\n- Added routes configuration for integration with OpenMRS.\n\n* feat: Update yarn.lock to include chatbot agent and display packages with dependencies\n\n* feat: Update CI workflows to include develop branch and remove hourly schedule for dependency updates\n\n* feat: Update README to include DHTI project details, setup instructions, and contributing guidelines\n\n* feat: Update CI workflows to use workflow_dispatch and add main.yml for build process\n\n* feat: Add axios as a dependency in package.json\n\n* Implement feature X to enhance user experience and fix bug Y in module Z\n\n* Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpZON7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1z8QAAhVlfqeImpetwPGSia9W7M2\n9621PvnW86qCO+/YfPkBBs+ITs/jgGD48quKem6OpQlX5Ma4Fv3PmvXTyKO/2/lq\nAd41/zIHRyCzOaxGN6cCzmFniHbgS0ezJI4rcnajlYVgxSxlGPS6h5elNIA96yKB\nsHpG9vZrDfgles+lqTHipwlSEw+fevBYGinzxOtVjNCVRQf8+LLy0HOVtU2gFQ