tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commit/739dc413ba328d43a7cb61122418de0a39c90197","node_id":"C_kwDOQ4CY7doAKDczOWRjNDEzYmEzMjhkNDNhN2NiNjExMjI0MThkZTBhMzljOTAxOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commit/e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35","sha":"e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commits/e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35"}],"sha":"739dc413ba328d43a7cb61122418de0a39c90197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commits/739dc413ba328d43a7cb61122418de0a39c90197"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7460895?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand","id":7460895,"login":"Ujjawal-Anand","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjA4OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commits/e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T07:25:13Z","email":"ujjawalanand1729@gmail.com","name":"ujjawal-anand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T07:25:13Z","email":"ujjawalanand1729@gmail.com","name":"ujjawal-anand"},"message":"feat: implement complete Menu Management system with Categories and Menu Items\n\nImplemented comprehensive menu management functionality for restaurants, including category organization and full menu item CRUD operations with options, addons, and availability management.\n\n## Backend Implementation (Restaurant Service)\n\n### Domain Layer\n- Created Category entity with business validation (name length, sort order)\n- Updated MenuItem entity with availability management methods\n- Added Category repository interface\n- Updated MenuItemRepository interface to support string status\n\n### Application Layer - Category Use Cases\n- CreateCategoryUseCase: Create categories with duplicate name prevention\n- GetCategoryUseCase: Retrieve category by ID with error handling\n- ListCategoriesUseCase: List all categories for a restaurant (sorted)\n- UpdateCategoryUseCase: Update category name, description, sort order, active status\n- DeleteCategoryUseCase: Delete category with menu item validation\n\n### Application Layer - MenuItem Use Cases\n- GetMenuItemUseCase: Retrieve menu item by ID\n- ListMenuItemsUseCase: Search/filter menu items by restaurant, category, status, dietary options\n- UpdateMenuItemUseCase: Update menu item details (price, description, flags)\n- DeleteMenuItemUseCase: Delete menu item\n- UpdateMenuItemAvailabilityUseCase: Quick availability status updates\n\n### Infrastructure Layer\n- CategoryRepository implementation with TypeORM\n- Proper domain/entity mapping for categories\n- Query optimization with sort order\n\n### Presentation Layer\n- Added 11 new gRPC endpoints in RestaurantController\n  - Category: Create, Get, List, Update, Delete\n  - MenuItem: Get, List, Update, Delete\n  - Already existed: CreateMenuItem\n- Added toCategoryResponse mapper with timestamp conversion\n- Updated RestaurantModule with all new providers\n\n### Proto Updates\n- Added GetCategory RPC method\n- Copied updated proto to shared and gateway locations\n\n## GraphQL Gateway Integration\n\n### Schema Extensions\n- Added 175+ lines of new types and operations\n- Category types: Category, CreateCategoryInput, UpdateCategoryInput, CategoriesResponse\n- MenuItem types: MenuItem, MenuItemStatus enum, DietaryOption enum\n- Complex types: NutritionalInfo, MenuItemOption, OptionChoice, MenuItemAddon\n- Added MenuItemsResponse with pagination\n\n### Query Operations\n- category(id): Get single category\n- categories(restaurantId): List all categories for restaurant\n- menuItem(id): Get single menu item with full details\n- menuItems(...filters): Search/filter menu items with pagination\n\n### Mutation Operations\n- createCategory: Create new category (owner only)\n- updateCategory: Update category (owner only)\n- deleteCategory: Delete empty category (owner only)\n- createMenuItem: Create menu item with options/addons (owner only)\n- updateMenuItem: Update menu item details (owner only)\n- deleteMenuItem: Delete menu item (owner only)\n- updateMenuItemAvailability: Quick availability updates (owner only)\n\n### gRPC Client\n- Added 10 new promisified service methods\n- Category methods: create, get, list, update, delete\n- MenuItem methods: create, get, list, update, delete\n\n### Resolvers\n- Implemented all 11 resolver functions with:\n  - Authentication checks for mutations\n  - Ownership verification (restaurant owner check)\n  - Bidirectional case conversion (camelCase ↔ snake_case)\n  - Protobuf timestamp conversion\n  - Proper error handling and messages\n  - Enum mapping for status values\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Category Management\n- Hierarchical menu organization\n- Sort order control for display\n- Active/inactive toggle\n- Duplicate name prevention per restaurant\n- Cannot delete categories with menu items\n\n### Menu Item Management\n- Full CRUD operations\n- Complex pricing with discounts\n- Options and choices (e.g., size, toppings)\n- Addons with max quantities\n- Dietary information (vegetarian, vegan, allergens)\n- Nutritional information\n- Availability status (AVAILABLE, OUT_OF_STOCK, DISCONTINUED)\n- Preparation time estimates\n- Popular/New item flags\n- Multiple images support\n\n### Security & Authorization\n- All mutations require authentication\n- Restaurant ownership verification\n- Prevents unauthorized menu modifications\n\n### Data Validation\n- Category name validation (1-100 chars)\n- Price must be > 0\n- Vegan items must be vegetarian\n- Discounted price cannot exceed regular price\n- Cannot mark discontinued items as available\n\n## Documentation\n\nCreated comprehensive MENU-MANAGEMENT-EXAMPLES.md with:\n- Step-by-step curl examples for all operations\n- Complete menu setup flow example\n- Error scenario examples\n- Environment variable setup\n- Multiple filtering examples (by category, status, dietary options)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Fixed TypeScript compilation error (MenuItemStatus type)\n- Services rebuilt and tested successfully\n- All gRPC endpoints functional\n- GraphQL schema validated\n- Resolvers tested with authentication\n\n## File Changes\n\n**New Files**:\n- Category domain entity and repository (2 files)\n- 11 new use case files (Category + MenuItem)\n- MENU-MANAGEMENT-EXAMPLES.md documentation\n\n**Modified Files**:\n- restaurant.controller.ts: +100 lines (11 new endpoints)\n- restaurant.module.ts: Updated with 11 new providers\n- restaurant.graphql: +175 lines (types, queries, mutations)\n- restaurant.resolver.ts: +200 lines (11 new resolvers)\n- restaurant-service.client.ts: +90 lines (10 new methods)\n- Proto files: Added GetCategory RPC\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb66d0e89d8fb19f30881d0e98947e4dff8ebb41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/git/trees/fb66d0e89d8fb19f30881d0e98947e4dff8ebb41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/git/commits/e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7460895?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand","id":7460895,"login":"Ujjawal-Anand","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjA4OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commit/e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35","node_id":"C_kwDOQ4CY7doAKGU4MTMxZTIxYWZjZmQ4ZTM1OGFlMjY5OWM5OGJhZTA4MTk5ZDBiMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commit/4630ec42da571f5c4fbf70587475cf36a80f9fae","sha":"4630ec42da571f5c4fbf70587475cf36a80f9fae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commits/4630ec42da571f5c4fbf70587475cf36a80f9fae"}],"sha":"e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commits/e8131e21afcfd8e358ae2699c98bae08199d0b35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7460895?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ujjawal-Anand","id":7460895,"login":"Ujjawal-Anand","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NjA4OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ujjawal-Anand","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ujjawal-Anand/tga-case-study/commits/4630ec42da571f5c4fbf70587475cf36a80f9fae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-12T07:04:23Z","email":"ujjawalanand1729@gmail.com","name":"ujjawal-anand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-12T07:04:23Z","email":"ujjawalanand1729@gmail.com","name":"ujjawal-anand"},"message":"feat: implement Restaurant Service with GraphQL Gateway integration\n\nCompleted NestJS Restaurant Service with Clean Architecture and integrated with GraphQL Gateway for complete CRUD operations.\n\n## Restaurant Service (NestJS)\n- Implemented Clean Architecture with domain-driven design\n- Created Restaurant aggregate root with value objects (BusinessInfo, Location, DeliveryInfo)\n- Added TypeORM entities with JSONB columns for nested data structures\n- Implemented CRUD use cases (Create, Get, Search, Update, Delete)\n- Fixed TypeORM UUID type configuration for foreign keys\n- Added protobuf Timestamp conversion with proper null handling\n- Made license_expiry optional in domain and entity layers\n- Set up PostgreSQL database with migrations\n\n## GraphQL Gateway Integration\n- Created comprehensive GraphQL schema (200+ lines) for restaurant operations\n- Implemented gRPC client for Restaurant Service communication\n- Built GraphQL resolvers with bidirectional case conversion (camelCase ↔ snake_case)\n- Added protobuf Timestamp ↔ ISO string conversion in resolvers\n- Integrated authentication middleware with ownership verification\n- Combined User and Restaurant schemas in unified gateway\n- Fixed case conversion to handle numbers (address_line_1 ↔ addressLine1)\n\n## Key Bug Fixes\n- Fixed TypeORM UUID columns (changed from varchar(255) to uuid type)\n- Added null safety for date.toISOString() calls to prevent \"Invalid time value\" errors\n- Enhanced case conversion regex to handle numbers after underscores\n- Fixed authentication context checks (context.user → context.isAuthenticated)\n- Implemented proper protobuf Timestamp helpers in both gateway and service\n\n## Testing\n- Added test files for restaurant creation and GraphQL queries\n- Verified end-to-end flow: auth → create restaurant → persist to DB → search\n- Tested ownership verification for update/delete operations\n- Validated timestamp conversion in both directions\n\n## Documentation\n- Updated CURRENT-STATE-SUMMARY.md with complete restaurant service documentation\n- Added restaurant creation flow walkthrough\n- Included curl examples for testing restaurant operations\n- Documented technical highlights and lessons learned\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fccf08da010a97