7f89e6ea3f31b676364d3c9ca70403cde54308ba","sha":"7f89e6ea3f31b676364d3c9ca70403cde54308ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/7f89e6ea3f31b676364d3c9ca70403cde54308ba"}],"sha":"f5b159ee3c590dd67ac1fb03befb2826c3a00e48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/f5b159ee3c590dd67ac1fb03befb2826c3a00e48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/ea50dd9b5ad884d9f49d6cfcdd04cfe980d96775/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:07:51Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:07:51Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): judge every implementation commit''s author and committer before the push\n\nReview of #1865 at 756e37033. The mint made aria-implementer the request\nworktree''s default identity, but a default is not a perimeter. git''s\nauthor.*/committer.* keys outrank user.* in every scope and\nGIT_AUTHOR_*/GIT_COMMITTER_* outrank both. The sandbox''s HOME is a\nwritable tmpfs, and the agent runs code it wrote (pytest, npm test, nx\ntest, python3 <file>.py), so a commit by someone else was reachable from\ninside the sandbox even though `git config`, `--author` and `-S` are\nrefused at the command line. Measured: `[author] name=Evil` in the HOME\nconfig commits as Evil, while the committer stays aria-implementer.\nNothing downstream compared either.\n\nN1. The pre-PR-open perimeter gains its 21st check,\ncommit_identity_is_the_kernels (implementation_safety, GATE_PRE_PR_OPEN).\nOn a machine-approved branch, every commit base..tip must have\nIMPLEMENTER_COMMIT_IDENTITY as author AND committer. Otherwise the\ndelivery is refused at pre_pr_open with\n`commit_identity_foreign:<sha>:<role>=<ident>`: nothing pushed, no lease\nminted, no gh call.\n- pr_manager derives the expected identity from the proposal''s approval\n  source. A machine approval is minted only by\n  apply_engine.stage_converged_plan_for_pr, for the action the executor''s\n  implementer commits on. An operator approval is a person''s change and\n  declares none, as does the self-revert opener.\n- _branch_commits_for_action now also reads author and committer, in the\n  format implementation_identity owns (COMMIT_IDENTS_LOG_FORMAT).\n- The comparison has one owner, implementation_identity.\n  foreign_commit_identities, shared by the perimeter and the containment\n  probe. The probe''s inline copy is gone.\n- The check lives in the perimeter that prepare_pr_open already runs, so\n  implementation_delivery and tools/aria-poc/ci_executor.py are untouched\n  (ARIA-HIGH-388 owns delivery_admission_refusal and the executor''s\n  settlement call sites).\n\nN3. mint_signing_key(commit_identity=...) raises\nCommitIdentityScopeRefused (a ValueError, the class the holders already\ncatch) unless the workspace is a linked worktree. The refusal comes\nbefore the key, the snapshot or any config write, so a main checkout''s\nshared --local config can never receive an identity that every worktree,\nthe operator''s included, would commit as.\n\nN2. The real spawn keeps the system config layer; I did not set\nGIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null on it.\n- The system layer is root-owned, so the agent cannot plant anything in\n  it, and on this runner there is no /etc/gitconfig at all.\n- It is the layer a host uses for policy the contained toolchains rely on\n  (safe.directory, http.sslCAInfo behind a proxy, credential and URL\n  rewrites for npm/cargo git dependencies). Dropping it would change\n  every agent and validation spawn, not only their identity.\n- The identity itself is now judged on the commits, whatever layer\n  supplied it: a system author.* or user.* would be refused by N1 like\n  any other foreign ident.\n- The hold and the probe still point both ambient layers at /dev/null.\n  Their job is to prove that the tree''s own config carries the identity,\n  which is the stricter question.\n\nB1. tests/invariants/v9/test_phase_v9_0_c_gh_token_factory.py pins\ngh_token_factory.__all__. I missed it because my first sweep grepped only\nthe top level of aria-kernel/tests. It now includes GitCommitIdentity and\nCommitIdentityScopeRefused, and the v9_0_d registry pins grow to 21\nchecks with a refusing case for the new one. The sweep is now derived\nfrom the whole tests tree, invariants included, plus every test that\nimports a helper touching these modules.\n\nFixtures that stand in for the implementer''s commit (implementation\ndelivery, the merge seam, the pr_manager e2e chain) now commit through\ngit_fixtures.implementer_identity_args(), as the hold''s identity does in\nproduction. New tests:\n- a planted [author] in the HOME config, and GIT_COMMITTER_* in the\n  environment, each refused by name while a kernel-identity commit passes;\n- a foreign-author commit refused at pre_pr_open before any push, lease\n  or gh call;\n- a main checkout refused an identity with nothing written.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-implementer-commit-identity.md#ARIA-HIGH-387","tree":{"sha":"2c5c46a6718dfe26e60b25a3856f056c2e305701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/2c5c46a6718dfe26e60b25a3856f056c2e305701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/ea50dd9b5ad884d9f49d6cfcdd04cfe980d96775","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c5c46a6718dfe26e60b25a3856f056c2e305701\nparent 756e370332ba84f18f14a9380140e247f64075c1\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791454071 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791454071 +0200\n\nfix(aria): judge every implementation commit''s author and committer before the push\n\nReview of #1865 at 756e37033. The mint made aria-implementer the request\nworktree''s default identity, but a default is not a perimeter. git''s\nauthor.*/committer.* keys outrank user.* in every scope and\nGIT_AUTHOR_*/GIT_COMMITTER_* outrank both. The sandbox''s HOME is a\nwritable tmpfs, and the agent runs code it wrote (pytest, npm test, nx\ntest, python3 <file>.py), so a commit by someone else was reachable from\ninside the sandbox even though `git config`, `--author` and `-S` are\nrefused at the command line. Measured: `[author] name=Evil` in the HOME\nconfig commits as Evil, while the committer stays aria-implementer.\nNothing downstream compared either.\n\nN1. The pre-PR-open perimeter gains its 21st check,\ncommit_identity_is_the_kernels (implementation_safety, GATE_PRE_PR_OPEN).\nOn a machine-approved branch, every commit base..tip must have\nIMPLEMENTER_COMMIT_IDENTITY as author AND committer. Otherwise the\ndelivery is refused at pre_pr_open with\n`commit_identity_foreign:<sha>:<role>=<ident>`: nothing pushed, no lease\nminted, no gh call.\n- pr_manager derives the expected identity from the proposal''s approval\n  source. A machine approval is minted only by\n  apply_engine.stage_converged_plan_for_pr, for the action the executor''s\n  implementer commits on. An operator approval is a person''s change and\n  declares none, as does the self-revert opener.\n- _branch_commits_for_action now also reads author and committer, in the\n  format implementation_identity owns (COMMIT_IDENTS_LOG_FORMAT).\n- The comparison has one owner, implementation_identity.\n  foreign_commit_identities, shared by the perimeter and the containment\n  probe. The probe''s inline copy is gone.\n- The check lives in the perimeter that prepare_pr_open already runs, so\n  implementation_delivery and tools/aria-poc/ci_executor.py are untouched\n  (ARIA-HIGH-388 owns delivery_admission_refusal and the executor''s\n  settlement call sites).\n\nN3. mint_signing_key(commit_identity=...) raises\nCommitIdentityScopeRefused (a ValueError, the class the holders already\ncatch) unless the workspace is a linked worktree. The refusal comes\nbefore the key, the snapshot or any config write, so a main checkout''s\nshared --local config can never receive an identity that every worktree,\nthe operator''s included, would commit as.\n\nN2. The real spawn keeps the system config layer; I did not set\nGIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null on it.\n- The system layer is root-owned, so the agent cannot plant anything in\n  it, and on this runner there is no /etc/gitconfig at all.\n- It is the layer a host uses for policy the contained toolchains rely on\n  (safe.directory, http.sslCAInfo behind a proxy, credential and URL\n  rewrites for npm/cargo git dependencies). Dropping it would change\n  every agent and validation spawn, not only their identity.\n- The identity itself is now judged on the commits, whatever layer\n  supplied it: a system author.* or user.* would be refused by N1 like\n  any other foreign ident.\n- The hold and the probe still point both ambient layers at /dev/null.\n  Their job is to prove that the tree''s own config carries the identity,\n  which is the stricter question.\n\nB1. tests/invariants/v9/test_phase_v9_0_c_gh_token_factory.py pins\ngh_token_factory.__all__. I missed it because my first sweep grepped only\nthe top level of aria-kernel/tests. It now includes GitCommitIdentity and\nCommitIdentityScopeRefused, and the v9_0_d registry pins grow to 21\nchecks with a refusing case for the new one. The sweep is now derived\nfrom the whole tests tree, invariants included, plus every test that\nimports a helper touching these modules.\n\nFixtures that stand in for the implementer''s commit (implementation\ndelivery, the merge seam, the pr_manager e2e chain) now commit through\ngit_fixtures.implementer_identity_args(), as the hold''s identity does in\nproduction. New tests:\n- a planted [author] in the HOME config, and GIT_COMMITTER_* in the\n  environment, each refused by name while a kernel-identity commit passes;\n- a foreign-author commit refused at pre_pr_open before any push, lease\n  or gh call;\n- a main checkout refused an identity with nothing written.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-implementer-commit-identity.md#ARIA-HIGH-387\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHpxzzrFI0apW62bY7fzkERPiPd0SBsRrTQuikOsXIXC+ZukX//INei+A/rXTRrqpZ\noXYhNTL7Psn2GTbRU5xA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T10:13:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https:/