83b4d904d44cd391eab15d877aa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/f6b451ae3ff983b4d904d44cd391eab15d877aa9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/89fbd52589c9cf710a6a475d1c8d31bf75a1c740/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:42:53Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:42:53Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): name an unnameable evidence path instead of raising\n\nThe re-review of PR #1863 at 3cb471a28 found the drain could wedge again,\nthrough the same class of crash.\n\n- evidence_trust.stat_evidence_path became the only stat the evidence\n  law makes, and it caught only OSError.\n- os.stat raises ValueError for an embedded NUL, and\n  UnicodeEncodeError (also a ValueError) for a lone surrogate.\n  Path.exists used to swallow both.\n- Both survive JSON decoding of an MCP runtime signal''s code_refs\n  (\\u0000, \\ud800). The shape law admitted them, so split_citable_refs\n  kept them as evidence.\n- The ValueError then escaped the drain''s OSError containment. The same\n  raise reached the submit law, the classifier and the tool-output\n  check.\n\nThe fix:\n\n- stat_evidence_path catches ValueError at the stat call only, as\n  unresolvable (embedded_nul or unencodable).\n- agent_ref_shape_refusal refuses C0/C1 control characters and\n  unencodable paths as agent_evidence_path_unresolvable. Such a ref\n  never reaches evidence, and the encodability check now runs before\n  the component-length check, which would itself have raised on a\n  surrogate.\n\nA property test runs every C0/C1 control character and two surrogates\nthrough the shape law, the submit law, the classifier, the tool-output\ncheck and pressure routing. The reviewer''s NUL reproduction (and its\nsurrogate twin) runs through the drain. 64 checks fail on 3cb471a28.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-pressure-state-evidence.md#ARIA-HIGH-384","tree":{"sha":"3a49468a965dd5a6603165346309d66551ca5396","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/3a49468a965dd5a6603165346309d66551ca5396"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/89fbd52589c9cf710a6a475d1c8d31bf75a1c740","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a49468a965dd5a6603165346309d66551ca5396\nparent 3cb471a28dd41a4e2d99f8ff099d0d96ae1cf539\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791452573 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791452573 +0200\n\nfix(aria): name an unnameable evidence path instead of raising\n\nThe re-review of PR #1863 at 3cb471a28 found the drain could wedge again,\nthrough the same class of crash.\n\n- evidence_trust.stat_evidence_path became the only stat the evidence\n  law makes, and it caught only OSError.\n- os.stat raises ValueError for an embedded NUL, and\n  UnicodeEncodeError (also a ValueError) for a lone surrogate.\n  Path.exists used to swallow both.\n- Both survive JSON decoding of an MCP runtime signal''s code_refs\n  (\\u0000, \\ud800). The shape law admitted them, so split_citable_refs\n  kept them as evidence.\n- The ValueError then escaped the drain''s OSError containment. The same\n  raise reached the submit law, the classifier and the tool-output\n  check.\n\nThe fix:\n\n- stat_evidence_path catches ValueError at the stat call only, as\n  unresolvable (embedded_nul or unencodable).\n- agent_ref_shape_refusal refuses C0/C1 control characters and\n  unencodable paths as agent_evidence_path_unresolvable. Such a ref\n  never reaches evidence, and the encodability check now runs before\n  the component-length check, which would itself have raised on a\n  surrogate.\n\nA property test runs every C0/C1 control character and two surrogates\nthrough the shape law, the submit law, the classifier, the tool-output\ncheck and pressure routing. The reviewer''s NUL reproduction (and its\nsurrogate twin) runs through the drain. 64 checks fail on 3cb471a28.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-pressure-state-evidence.md#ARIA-HIGH-384\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJGdb+PsBMdQOHhAqg14gx+hmUxtUtqgSTFZ0aHtcNOFOctHZ2QUFgLwkdngpEUXam\nL7Ns2/rK7uCUBJVLamFAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:49:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/89fbd52589c9cf710a6a475d1c8d31bf75a1c740","node_id":"C_kwDOQ4Ocb9oAKDg5ZmJkNTI1ODljOWNmNzEwYTZhNDc1ZDFjOGQzMWJmNzVhMWM3NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/3cb471a28dd41a4e2d99f8ff099d0d96ae1cf539","sha":"3cb471a28dd41a4e2d99f8ff099d0d96ae1cf539","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/3cb471a28dd41a4e2d99f8ff099d0d96ae1cf539"}],"sha":"89fbd52589c9cf710a6a475d1c8d31bf75a1c740","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/89fbd52589c9cf710a6a475d1c8d31bf75a1c740"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/c2f09cea395007fe7ae74dd221692bcd97a7a800/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:19:46Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:19:46Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"security(platform): tenant erasure binds the erased tenant''s RLS context, so it deletes what its proof attests\n\nTenantErasureTargetExecutor ran every transaction with no tenant bound. All\nerasure targets run RlsModule.forPoolService, whose checkout leaves an empty\ntenant with bypass off, so under FORCE RLS and a NOBYPASSRLS role every\nerasure DELETE, post-erasure hook, proof read and outbox write matched zero\nrows while the hook names went into the proof hash. #1805''s route-table purge\nmade this reachable for sensor-service.\n\nEvery executor transaction (proof pre-check, erasure, replay, blocked and\nfailure emission) now opens through one helper that calls\nbindTenantRlsContext for the erased tenant before anything else and reads the\nbinding back. Hooks return the rows or keys they removed; the executor logs\neach count and folds hook:count into the proof hash, so a hook that removed\nnothing is visible. No consumer recomputes the hash, so the proof shape is\nunchanged; the crypto-shred hook reports 1 or 0 destroyed keys. Real-Postgres\nspecs cover both modes (sensor tenant-schema-module with both route tables,\nconfig source-schema-tenant-column) and fail with the binding removed.\n\nThe provisioning-key claim now re-checks is_active and expiry next to\nmax_devices in one UPDATE and requires exactly one claimed row, so a key\nrevoked or expired mid self-register registers nothing.\n\nRegistered SENSOR-MEDIUM-180 (no per-username failure limiter before PBKDF2).\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-06-edge-mqtt-auth-rls.md#PLAT-CRITICAL-923\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-06-edge-mqtt-auth-rls.md#SENSOR-LOW-181\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-06-edge-mqtt-auth-rls.md#SENSOR-CRITICAL-143","tree":{"sha":"ff0cecb9e9b6845111d4e2b8b77f6f2c3566645e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/ff0cecb9e9b6845111d4e2b8b77f6f2c3566645e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/c2f09cea395007fe7ae74dd221692bcd97a7a800","verification":{"payload":"tree ff0cecb9e9b6845111d4e2b8b77f6f2c3566645e\nparent 1df32814551efe16ca3e3be45c08f6c2c0f39535\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791451186 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791451186 +0200\n\nsecurity(platform): tenant erasure binds the erased tenant''s RLS context, so it deletes what its proof attests\n\nTenantErasureTargetExecutor ran every transaction with no tenant bound. All\nerasure targets run RlsModule.forPoolService, whose checkout leaves an empty\ntenant with bypass off, so under FORCE RLS and a NOBYPASSRLS role every\nerasure DELETE, post-erasure hook, proof read and outbox write matched zero\nrows while the hook names went into the proof hash. #1805''s route-table purge\nmade this reachable for sensor-service.\n\nEvery executor transaction (proof pre-check, erasure, replay, blocked and\nfailure emission) now opens through one helper that calls\nbindTenantRlsContext for the erased tenant before anything else and reads the\nbinding back. Hooks return the rows or keys they removed; the executor logs\neach count and folds hook:count into the proof hash, so a hook that removed\nnothing is visible. No consumer recomputes the hash, so the proof shape is\nunchanged; the crypto-shred hook reports 1 or 0 destroyed keys. Real-Postgres\nspecs cover both modes (sensor tenant-schema-module with both route tables,\nconfig source-schema-tenant-column) and fail with the binding removed.\n\nThe provisioning-key claim now re-checks is_active and expiry next to\nmax_devices in one UPDATE and requires exactly one claimed row, so a key\nrevoked or expired mid self-register registers nothing.\n\nRegistered SENSOR-MEDIUM-180 (no per-username failure limiter before PBKDF2).\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-06-edge-mqtt-auth-rls.md#PLAT-CRITICAL-923\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-06-edge-mqtt-auth-rls.md#SENSOR-LOW-181\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-06-edge-mqtt-auth-rls.md#SENSOR-CRITICAL-143\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDpaRhyc/sQvLHllzKv8s6s221LxbUl+brkgtifYmQlTBRzKHYnHNflrtYmhxTjJQu\nqpwK1ukSD7XlMzhBtC6AM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:24:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/c2f09cea395007