d708f7390","sha":"475d6dec716804ceb6813693e710658d708f7390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/475d6dec716804ceb6813693e710658d708f7390"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/cda7c692a4fbf39fd443751377bf3444508cc149","sha":"cda7c692a4fbf39fd443751377bf3444508cc149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/cda7c692a4fbf39fd443751377bf3444508cc149"}],"sha":"fd5981a0518b9296868a485ad6bc266b3d78899f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/fd5981a0518b9296868a485ad6bc266b3d78899f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/cda7c692a4fbf39fd443751377bf3444508cc149/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:54:22Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:54:22Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): provision the Rust toolchain the tree declares in both room-building lanes\n\nThe first plan ARIA converged without an operator (F-013,\nplan-cyc-20261007T225133Z-auto) never reached its implementer. Executor\nrun 37713931273 refused it before the spawn with\n`validation_toolchain_unresolvable:cargo`. The validation room binds\nevery toolchain the tree declares, and the root Cargo.toml declares\ncargo and rustc. No ARIA lane provisioned Rust, and the self-hosted\nrunner had none, so every delivery was refused at admission whatever it\nchanged. So was every self-revert and branch-update validation in the\ncycle lane, which builds the same room.\n\nThe room''s refusal is correct; the lanes were the fault. Both now call\nthe setup-rust-workspace action the CI lanes already use. The pinned\nchannel, components and targets come from one manifest. The action puts\n$CARGO_HOME/bin on the PATH the room resolves on, and its verify fails\nthe job by name if the toolchain is wrong.\n\nI-SBX-05 reads the declared toolchains from the kernel''s\nvalidation_toolchains_for. It fails when a declared toolchain has no\nprovisioner, or when a room-building lane omits that provisioner or runs\nit after the room is built. It fails on main and passes here.\n\nThe runner user was provisioned by hand once: rustup with 1.88.0\n(minimal profile, plus rustfmt, clippy, rust-src and the manifest''s\nthree targets). Reproduced and verified on the runner as gharunner:\nwithout ~/.cargo/bin the room is refused; with it, the room builds and\nbinds the pinned toolchain.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-runner-rust-toolchain.md#ARIA-HIGH-383","tree":{"sha":"b6fc1a4bf6da5f2d91581deb9cfca89224744b59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/b6fc1a4bf6da5f2d91581deb9cfca89224744b59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/cda7c692a4fbf39fd443751377bf3444508cc149","verification":{"payload":"tree b6fc1a4bf6da5f2d91581deb9cfca89224744b59\nparent 475d6dec716804ceb6813693e710658d708f7390\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791435262 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791435262 +0200\n\nfix(aria): provision the Rust toolchain the tree declares in both room-building lanes\n\nThe first plan ARIA converged without an operator (F-013,\nplan-cyc-20261007T225133Z-auto) never reached its implementer. Executor\nrun 37713931273 refused it before the spawn with\n`validation_toolchain_unresolvable:cargo`. The validation room binds\nevery toolchain the tree declares, and the root Cargo.toml declares\ncargo and rustc. No ARIA lane provisioned Rust, and the self-hosted\nrunner had none, so every delivery was refused at admission whatever it\nchanged. So was every self-revert and branch-update validation in the\ncycle lane, which builds the same room.\n\nThe room''s refusal is correct; the lanes were the fault. Both now call\nthe setup-rust-workspace action the CI lanes already use. The pinned\nchannel, components and targets come from one manifest. The action puts\n$CARGO_HOME/bin on the PATH the room resolves on, and its verify fails\nthe job by name if the toolchain is wrong.\n\nI-SBX-05 reads the declared toolchains from the kernel''s\nvalidation_toolchains_for. It fails when a declared toolchain has no\nprovisioner, or when a room-building lane omits that provisioner or runs\nit after the room is built. It fails on main and passes here.\n\nThe runner user was provisioned by hand once: rustup with 1.88.0\n(minimal profile, plus rustfmt, clippy, rust-src and the manifest''s\nthree targets). Reproduced and verified on the runner as gharunner:\nwithout ~/.cargo/bin the room is refused; with it, the room builds and\nbinds the pinned toolchain.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-runner-rust-toolchain.md#ARIA-HIGH-383\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfF