":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/031c9e4b01c121609f1c660dc36092a5af5c5d56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/5613f6aa3a49f791480cf87630b19cf7394ea557/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:42:55Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:42:55Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): report cargo and pytest test surfaces, say \"not modelled\" when unread\n\nReview of #1859 (MEDIUM-2). The test surface read only nx manifests, so every\nRust project and the Python kernel rendered \"test targets: none\", a false\nexplicit negative of exactly the kind ARIA-MEDIUM-382 is about. Cargo.toml now\nyields a `cargo test` target with tests/ files and #[cfg(test)] modules as\nspecs; a pytest manifest, pytest.ini or tests/ of test_*.py yields `pytest`.\nA project with no manifest the map reads renders \"not modelled\", never \"none\".\n\nThe spec inventory is one pruned os.walk (0.26 s here), and _iter_test_files\nreplaces four rglob passes that walked every node_modules tree before\nfiltering with one pruned walk of the same result set (0.08 s), so a non-noop\nrefresh no longer pays for the dependency tree.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-MEDIUM-382","tree":{"sha":"ee442e119885cce7220be31be03be147fe001310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/ee442e119885cce7220be31be03be147fe001310"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/5613f6aa3a49f791480cf87630b19cf7394ea557","verification":{"payload":"tree ee442e119885cce7220be31be03be147fe001310\nparent e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791420175 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791420175 +0200\n\nfix(aria): report cargo and pytest test surfaces, say \"not modelled\" when unread\n\nReview of #1859 (MEDIUM-2). The test surface read only nx manifests, so every\nRust project and the Python kernel rendered \"test targets: none\", a false\nexplicit negative of exactly the kind ARIA-MEDIUM-382 is about. Cargo.toml now\nyields a `cargo test` target with tests/ files and #[cfg(test)] modules as\nspecs; a pytest manifest, pytest.ini or tests/ of test_*.py yields `pytest`.\nA project with no manifest the map reads renders \"not modelled\", never \"none\".\n\nThe spec inventory is one pruned os.walk (0.26 s here), and _iter_test_files\nreplaces four rglob passes that walked every node_modules tree before\nfiltering with one pruned walk of the same result set (0.08 s), so a non-noop\nrefresh no longer pays for the dependency tree.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-MEDIUM-382\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQANmg6lxWz77qdk/d9FklA0c7Whfl3T/maH9gaAuUKNm2CiQWJlGuGNm+UWu+ypX4a\nseR+3yRLPCG9Rudjb4Xw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T00:47:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/5613f6aa3a49f791480cf87630b19cf7394ea557","node_id":"C_kwDOQ4Ocb9oAKDU2MTNmNmFhM2E0OWY3OTE0ODBjZjg3NjMwYjE5Y2Y3Mzk0ZWE1NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea","sha":"e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea"}],"sha":"5613f6aa3a49f791480cf87630b19cf7394ea557","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/5613f6aa3a49f791480cf87630b19cf7394ea557"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:42:11Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:42:11Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): derive write scope only from a defined copy side, follow a moved copy\n\nReview of #1859 (MEDIUM-1, MEDIUM-3). The derived split took a drift''s first\nevidence for every class and never read DRIFT_COPY_SIDES, so a cross-service\nenum_drift made its SQL side evidence, though the usual fix there is a\nmigration. DRIFT_COPY_SIDES ({\"ui_option_drift\": \"ui\"}) is now the one table of\nthe rule, with DRIFT_CLASS_SIDES pinned to the seeder''s side order; any class\nwithout a copy side, enum_drift included, stays undivided.\n\nA renamed copy file left only the contract grounded, so admission refused with\nfinding_write_scope_empty before the seed could re-ground it, and\nclosure_blocker called the finding unclosable. The split now reports\nfix_target_ungrounded; the unattended F source and closure_blocker admit on it\nwith an empty write set, and the seed splits on the copy the detector found\nnow (unverifiable without a detector). Operator requests still refuse by\nname: signed refs cannot follow a moved file. Also makes the review doc''s\nheadings unique (MD024) and adds the review corrections section.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-HIGH-381","tree":{"sha":"9f648e05224faea12573b3c82ffbad9fcd101ffa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/9f648e05224faea12573b3c82ffbad9fcd101ffa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f648e05224faea12573b3c82ffbad9fcd101ffa\nparent 7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791420131 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791420131 +0200\n\nfix(aria): derive write scope only from a defined copy side, follow a moved copy\n\nReview of #1859 (MEDIUM-1, MEDIUM-3). The derived split took a drift''s first\nevidence for every class and never read DRIFT_COPY_SIDES, so a cross-service\nenum_drift made its SQL side evidence, though the usual fix there is a\nmigration. DRIFT_COPY_SIDES ({\"ui_option_drift\": \"ui\"}) is now the one table of\nthe rule, with DRIFT_CLASS_SIDES pinned to the seeder''s side order; any class\nwithout a copy side, enum_drift included, stays undivided.\n\nA renamed copy file left only the contract grounded, so admission refused with\nfinding_write_scope_empty before the seed could re-ground it, and\nclosure_blocker called the finding unclosable. The split now reports\nfix_target_ungrounded; the unattended F source and closure_blocker admit on it\nwith an empty write set, and the seed splits on the copy the detector found\nnow (unverifiable without a detector). Operator requests still refuse by\nname: signed refs cannot follow a moved file. Also makes the review doc''s\nheadings unique (MD024) and adds the review corrections section.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-HIGH-381\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPVLmKr+igCsfo1j9vTxtSNjxHRT7dXWuSe3JQ6upRktNHgMgbgHBc9a3zXRfpl30Q\nBTgM3QuY6PllvmrPF2xQI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T00:47:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea","node_id":"C_kwDOQ4Ocb9oAKGUwMTVjNzdiYmUxYjFhM2ExOThiY2I0NTFhOWE5NjJiNzUxZTNjZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073","sha":"7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073"}],"sha":"e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/e015c77bbe1b1a3a198bcb451a9a962b751e3cea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:44:01Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:44:01Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): state every project''s test targets and specs on the repo map\n\nA round-2 cross-reviewer of F-015''s plan (CR-004) read the repository map''s\nsilence about web-hr-module as \"no spec, the runner may be unconfigured\".\nhr-module runs vitest as its package.json `test` script, nx infers it as the\nproject''s test target, and two specs under it passed that day. The map''s\nproject entries held root, dependencies and layer only, and the one test fact\nit had was per file; LeavesPage.tsx has no spec of its own, so nothing was\nsaid.\n\ntwin_test_surface reports, per project, the test targets nx resolves\n(project.json targets, then inferred package.json scripts, honouring\nnx.includedScripts) with their commands, and the spec files attributed by\nimpact_graph.project_for_path. Build and every refresh compute it with the same\nfunction, so a new spec or script cannot hide behind the graph cache. The map\nmoves to schema 2 (a v1 map is rebuilt whole). The blast-radius section of the\nprompt lists targets and specs, and says \"none\" in words; a row sealed from a\nv1 map renders unchanged.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-MEDIUM-382","tree":{"sha":"d2c56252213a420826eec1a968e27b9536820ddc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/d2c56252213a420826eec1a968e27b9536820ddc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073","verification":{"payload":"tree d2c56252213a420826eec1a968e27b9536820ddc\nparent 2ffc180f2b0485b46da2a22cbda666930b6dfb93\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791416641 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791416641 +0200\n\nfix(aria): state every project''s test targets and specs on the repo map\n\nA round-2 cross-reviewer of F-015''s plan (CR-004) read the repository map''s\nsilence about web-hr-module as \"no spec, the runner may be unconfigured\".\nhr-module runs vitest as its package.json `test` script, nx infers it as the\nproject''s test target, and two specs under it passed that day. The map''s\nproject entries held root, dependencies and layer only, and the one test fact\nit had was per file; LeavesPage.tsx has no spec of its own, so nothing was\nsaid.\n\ntwin_test_surface reports, per project, the test targets nx resolves\n(project.json targets, then inferred package.json scripts, honouring\nnx.includedScripts) with their commands, and the spec files attributed by\nimpact_graph.project_for_path. Build and every refresh compute it with the same\nfunction, so a new spec or script cannot hide behind the graph cache. The map\nmoves to schema 2 (a v1 map is rebuilt whole). The blast-radius section of the\nprompt lists targets and specs, and says \"none\" in words; a row sealed from a\nv1 map renders unchanged.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-MEDIUM-382\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJye2SglVGh0EqaY5qf6fqtfJ+QB3q3cP1qOGGIEWoDaot5vi4ShQtOictAMbVy6Aw\n9Kz+L3s25y1q4o8WPwCQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:48:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073","node_id":"C_kwDOQ4Ocb9oAKDdiMzBmNzBlYTI1YmRlYTI1ODIwMTg5YjgxYjJlMDk3MGRkODIwNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/2ffc180f2b0485b46da2a22cbda666930b6dfb93","sha":"2ffc180f2b0485b46da2a22cbda666930b6dfb93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/2ffc180f2b0485b46da2a22cbda666930b6dfb93"}],"sha":"7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/7b30f70ea25bdea25820189b81b2e0970dd82073"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/2ffc180f2b0485b46da2a22cbda666930b6dfb93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:39:09Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:39:09Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria): split a plan''s write scope from the evidence it cites\n\nF-015''s plan (plan-cyc-20261007T081056Z-auto) ended HUMAN_REQUIRED because\nadmission turned every file the finding cites into an affected surface. The\noperator declared the hr-service entity read-only evidence, yet it became a\nkey-change path, the round obligation pinned it, and staging would have handed\nit to the change ledger, which refuses an intended file a diff leaves alone.\nBoth planners narrowed the paths and the cross-reviewer flagged that in both\nrounds (CR-006).\n\nAdmission now splits grounded surfaces once (plan_write_scope): a signed\nwrite_roots list on the request when present, otherwise the finding''s own fix\ntarget (a drift''s copy side and its project), otherwise undivided. Only the\nwrite set becomes affected_surfaces and key-change paths; evidence_refs still\ncite everything. Admission scope v4 records the cited, unwritten files as\nevidence_surfaces: read-only in the bound even under a closure root, and part\nof every round''s read-only evidence scope. The obligation, allowed_scope and\nthe change ledger''s intended files therefore hold write scope only.\n\nRequests signed before write_roots existed (OP-F015) keep their bytes and use\nthe derivation; the recorder gains --write-root and refuses a boundary that\nleaves nothing to change.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-HIGH-381","tree":{"sha":"fd7d00bbd592b9a15da1b34275f1a93c07d90136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/fd7d00bbd592b9a15da1b34275f1a93c07d90136"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/2ffc180f2b0485b46da2a22cbda666930b6dfb93","verification":{"payload":"tree fd7d00bbd592b9a15da1b34275f1a93c07d90136\nparent 6bac3e8599a4d8f805858610558479fc3d92e0f5\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791416349 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791416349 +0200\n\nfix(aria): split a plan''s write scope from the evidence it cites\n\nF-015''s plan (plan-cyc-20261007T081056Z-auto) ended HUMAN_REQUIRED because\nadmission turned every file the finding cites into an affected surface. The\noperator declared the hr-service entity read-only evidence, yet it became a\nkey-change path, the round obligation pinned it, and staging would have handed\nit to the change ledger, which refuses an intended file a diff leaves alone.\nBoth planners narrowed the paths and the cross-reviewer flagged that in both\nrounds (CR-006).\n\nAdmission now splits grounded surfaces once (plan_write_scope): a signed\nwrite_roots list on the request when present, otherwise the finding''s own fix\ntarget (a drift''s copy side and its project), otherwise undivided. Only the\nwrite set becomes affected_surfaces and key-change paths; evidence_refs still\ncite everything. Admission scope v4 records the cited, unwritten files as\nevidence_surfaces: read-only in the bound even under a closure root, and part\nof every round''s read-only evidence scope. The obligation, allowed_scope and\nthe change ledger''s intended files therefore hold write scope only.\n\nRequests signed before write_roots existed (OP-F015) keep their bytes and use\nthe derivation; the recorder gains --write-root and refuses a boundary that\nleaves nothing to change.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-08-aria-plan-write-scope.md#ARIA-HIGH-381\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNX5NzUtpSXGfyRbZj7lhGeTRSzLn28T3WG0O7R7m/myzHOK/pN786ZsuGvv65UXqk\nx8AH0THQYWCOjJa4hWlgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:43:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/follow