,{"html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commit/048be8743414532712f15e59f45df006f7416938","sha":"048be8743414532712f15e59f45df006f7416938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/048be8743414532712f15e59f45df006f7416938"}],"sha":"08b6135bb309596098bd5b8a50f1d6a7944e7306","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/08b6135bb309596098bd5b8a50f1d6a7944e7306"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NDAxNzg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/513fe7d4f5e46fccd1963fd062971a86a1d9d343/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:08:13Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:08:13Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(sensor): a sensor records the tank it stands in; the description says where\n\nFarm binds water-chemistry inputs at a measurement point and checks the\nsensor stands there. For tanks that could not work: farm''s equipment\nlist presents tanks beside water equipment (isTank), a tank''s identity\nis tanks.id, and the registration wizard saved any pick as equipment_id\nand never set tank_id — every wizard-registered tank sensor had no tank.\nThe channel description also did not carry the equipment a device\nstands at.\n\n- devicePlacement: a picked tank becomes tankId, other water equipment\n  equipmentId; site/department/system changes clear both; the wizard\n  sends both (children already inherit the parent''s location).\n- The channel description carries equipmentId (contract field and\n  validator, SQL, GraphQL); location is the device owning the channel.\n- The registry marks loop-uniform quantities (temperature, salinity,\n  conductivity, specific conductance, alkalinity, calcium, hardness,\n  TDS) as loopHomogeneous, which farm''s resolver may inherit from a\n  system; DO, pH, CO2, nitrogen species and sulfide never are.\n\nNot changed: sensors registered earlier keep equipment_id = a tank id;\nfarm''s placement check accepts that legacy shape for a tank point.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-07-sensor-placement-identity.md#SENSOR-MEDIUM-172","tree":{"sha":"8b78decfb8c6b88f13cbae75417ad8089f34c7c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/8b78decfb8c6b88f13cbae75417ad8089f34c7c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/513fe7d4f5e46fccd1963fd062971a86a1d9d343","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b78decfb8c6b88f13cbae75417ad8089f34c7c4\nparent e377c083322a9e1260907c700e88807151b11c3b\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791400093 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791400093 +0200\n\nfix(sensor): a sensor records the tank it stands in; the description says where\n\nFarm binds water-chemistry inputs at a measurement point and checks the\nsensor stands there. For tanks that could not work: farm''s equipment\nlist presents tanks beside water equipment (isTank), a tank''s identity\nis tanks.id, and the registration wizard saved any pick as equipment_id\nand never set tank_id — every wizard-registered tank sensor had no tank.\nThe channel description also did not carry the equipment a device\nstands at.\n\n- devicePlacement: a picked tank becomes tankId, other water equipment\n  equipmentId; site/department/system changes clear both; the wizard\n  sends both (children already inherit the parent''s location).\n- The channel description carries equipmentId (contract field and\n  validator, SQL, GraphQL); location is the device owning the channel.\n- The registry marks loop-uniform quantities (temperature, salinity,\n  conductivity, specific conductance, alkalinity, calcium, hardness,\n  TDS) as loopHomogeneous, which farm''s resolver may inherit from a\n  system; DO, pH, CO2, nitrogen species and sulfide never are.\n\nNot changed: sensors registered earlier keep equipment_id = a tank id;\nfarm''s placement check accepts that legacy shape for a tank point.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-07-sensor-placement-identity.md#SENSOR-MEDIUM-172\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOzX4vIkcOMgrtmEIAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJG/ebuebVFkB/2My/PAs8WjcE7AJUAUq2Q2ZgQVFW06dYo3nCqfCzZAdNFfo5Wdhq\ngxXxSJZYxrAp/QkpeN9gI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:10:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77401788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Okan-wqm","id":77401788,"login":"Okan-wqm","node_id":"MDQ6