"https://api.github.com/users/Okan-wqm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/commits/eaf5bb6cb6cce087eced2314d81673579d937bf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:08:13Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:08:13Z","email":"77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"OKAN OZTURK"},"message":"fix(aria-kernel): merge main and admit its judge re-mints through the door\n\nMerges origin/main (#1825 ARIA-HIGH-360, #1826, #1836, train #1850) into\nthe request-admission branch. The door test found one new mint site:\njudge_remint.remint_judge_request, reached from the adjudication panel''s\nre_mint (remint_judge_for_panel) and the anchor-stale disposition\n(anchor_stale_effects.remint_judge). Both now carry an admission that\ninherits the dead judge''s recorded class (human_required_panel.remint*,\nanchor_stale.remint*). The executor convergence advance runs the drainer\n(plan steps, critical path; it never seeds) and the converged seam mints\nthrough the implementer (critical path), so neither needs a new class.\n\nReview of #1833, MEDIUM-5: remint_judge re-raises RequestAdmissionThrottled\nahead of its GovernanceError operator arm and the anchor-stale sweep\nrecords nothing for that request (throttled_retry): the next sweep\ndecides it again, and a throttle never becomes an operator escalation\nthat would feed the panels ARIA-HIGH-360 removed.\n\nConflicts: derive_request_states keeps main''s public ledgers= seam (the\nadmission measurement uses it); provider_outage stays the one admission\noutage predicate, which provider_clock (ARIA-HIGH-365) delegates to.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-07-aria-request-admission-budget.md#ARIA-HIGH-364","tree":{"sha":"d61c49b1c4c0dfadf09078f6624596598bf7dda4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/trees/d61c49b1c4c0dfadf09078f6624596598bf7dda4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Okan-wqm/aquaculture_platform/git/commits/eaf5bb6cb6cce087eced2314d81673579d937bf7","verification":{"payload":"tree d61c49b1c4c0dfadf09078f6624596598bf7dda4\nparent d062b41ded92cb69e1b26d8f9685a5252044eb7b\nparent d1ae49f42aedd0547b2afde7206c80cfe9833c0a\nauthor OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791400093 +0200\ncommitter OKAN OZTURK <77401788+Okan-wqm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791400093 +0200\n\nfix(aria-kernel): merge main and admit its judge re-mints through the door\n\nMerges origin/main (#1825 ARIA-HIGH-360, #1826, #1836, train #1850) into\nthe request-admission branch. The door test found one new mint site:\njudge_remint.remint_judge_request, reached from the adjudication panel''s\nre_mint (remint_judge_for_panel) and the anchor-stale disposition\n(anchor_stale_effects.remint_judge). Both now carry an admission that\ninherits the dead judge''s recorded class (human_required_panel.remint*,\nanchor_stale.remint*). The executor convergence advance runs the drainer\n(plan steps, critical path; it never seeds) and the converged seam mints\nthrough the implementer (critical path), so neither needs a new class.\n\nReview of #1833, MEDIUM-5: remint_judge re-raises RequestAdmissionThrottled\nahead of its GovernanceError operator arm and the anchor-stale sweep\nrecords nothing for that request (throttled_retry): the next sweep\ndecides it again, and a throttle never becomes an operator escalation\nthat would feed the panels ARIA-HIGH-360 removed.\n\nConflicts: derive_request_states keeps main''s public ledgers= seam (the\nadmission measurement uses it); provider_outage stays the one admission\noutage predicate, which provider_clock (ARIA-HIGH-365) delegates to.\n\nCloses: docs/reviews/claude/2026-10-07-aria-request-admission-budget.md#ARIA-HIGH-364\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgS9nW+eHMNSWNfFYQCzIGjH0vPV\nFOz